<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    v113 — Curio's cosmic launcher mark, applied from the designer's PNG
    (drawable-nodpi/ic_launcher_art.png, 2048×2048, the raster of the
    user-supplied art: a mint planet with a pink moon over layered pink and
    gold waves on a midnight navy→magenta sky, inside a rounded card with a
    white frame).

    The art is a ROUNDED CARD with a white frame and transparent corners —
    at the adaptive-icon canvas size (108dp) the card spans ~84–88%, which
    the launcher's mask (66dp safe zone) would crop: the frame, top stars
    and bottom waves were getting sliced ("broken / not properly placed").
    So the bitmap is inset 28dp on every side: the art fills the central
    52dp, the card lands at ~44×47dp — fully inside the safe circle, frame
    intact — floating on the full-bleed sky in ic_launcher_background.xml
    (whose gradient matches the card's own sky, so the two composite
    seamlessly behind the frame). The 2048px source downscales cleanly to
    every density.

    The SPLASH screen renders @drawable/ic_launcher_art directly (not this
    inset) so the full card art still fills the splash logo box.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:inset="28dp"
    android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_art" />
